       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as 850 mg three times daily. It would carry a high risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose or frequency\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
