       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it, and it could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis. A confirmation alone doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** That is the maximum standard dose of 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Enter a different dose you choose** that is within labeled limits.\n- **Help you escalate to pharmacy or the attending** if you think a non-standard dose is needed. They can review it and place the order through their own process.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it right away."
